.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt MOP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mop
.Nd use hardware-protected personal and shared CloudKit vaults
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Mop v6 generates device private keys in Secure Enclave. Personal vaults are the
one-member case of shared vaults. Every additional device requires explicit
owner approval. The application, AutoFill and CLI share device-local encrypted
checkpoints and device-only Keychain representations. There is no software-key
fallback, old-format reader, migration or portable recovery private key.
.Pp
Plaintext passwords and temporary record keys reach application memory.
Commands receiving a password receive plaintext. Removing access protects later
changes, but cannot erase copied secrets or old backups.
.Sh COMMANDS
Use
.Nm command --help
for complete arguments. Secret commands are read, write, list, delete, run,
inject and item. Values are supplied by hidden prompt or stdin, never positional
password arguments. References use mop://vault/item/[section/]field.
.Pp
Device request creates a public enrollment document; --recovery selects this
device's separate hardware recovery identity. Vault init creates a vault on this
device without recovery by default. Optional --recovery-request and --fingerprint
must be supplied together. Use replace-recovery to add hardware recovery later.
.Pp
Vault invite, accept and approve exchange public documents, independently
compared fingerprints/checkpoints and (for other accounts) a private iCloud
share URL. An iCloud invitation alone cannot decrypt the vault. Members,
remove-member, remove-device, role and reconcile-share manage access.
.Pp
Vault list includes trusted roots and untrusted iCloud enrollment hints. Rename changes references. Sync verifies
signed descendants and reconciles uncertain commits without replaying edits.
Export writes an encrypted checkpoint; import requires independent checkpoint
evidence and an already enrolled device.
.Pp
Vault recover runs on the enrolled hardware recovery device with a verified
backup and replacement public requests. --copy creates a new UUID/root under
the current account, preserving the source. Losing every authorized and recovery
device makes recovery impossible even with a backup.
.Pp
Vault delete requires --vault UUID --confirm UUID. It deletes the cloud zone;
existing local ciphertext and exported backups remain.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Fl -vault Ar NAME-OR-UUID
constrains selection. Management requires an explicit selection when multiple
vaults are registered.
.Pp
.Fl -offline
uses a previously verified checkpoint read-only. Remote revocation and
unobserved account changes cannot be detected offline.
.Pp
.Fl -state-directory Ar PATH
or MOP_STATE_DIRECTORY overrides device-local state. Never synchronize it.
.Sh SECURITY
Operational access requires a provisioned signed application, matching Keychain
access group/CloudKit environment, Secure Enclave and local authentication.
Every fill starts fresh authorization. GUI contexts last until lock/expiry;
hardware handles and individual secret keys are released after operations.
.Pp
Conflicting edits fail. Submitted operations may finish after cancellation;
journals and conditional version barriers determine their outcome. Do not
blindly repeat an uncertain mutation. No existing old-format data is deleted.
.Sh SEE ALSO
The project README, docs/SECURITY.md and docs/VAULT-NEXT-VALIDATION.md describe
workflows, precise platform boundaries and remaining physical-device checks.

.SH ICLOUD DEVICE ENROLLMENT
Use vault enrollment request on the new device, inbox on an existing owner,
status and confirm --code MATCHING_CODE on the new device, then approve --request-id UUID --code MATCHING_CODE on
the owner after comparing both displays. A final status finishes enrollment.
The app performs these exchanges automatically; explicit owner approval remains
required. Decline rejects a request. Requests expire after one day. This flow
is for the same Apple Account; sharing with another account remains separate.

Use enrollment restart on the new device to replace a stuck request without
replacing its hardware keys. Enrollment cancel stops the pending request.
Neither command deletes vault contents or revokes access already granted.
The app displays request status, expiry and the last successful iCloud check.
.SH DEVICE REMOVAL
.B mop vault devices
lists own-account devices across enrolled personal vaults.
.B mop vault devices --remove UUID
revokes a device across those vaults. The last owner device cannot be removed.
The removed device clears its local access after observing the signed revocation.
.B mop vault enrollment reconnect
explicitly permits fresh-key enrollment after removal; follow it with
.B mop vault enrollment request --vault UUID
while another owner device is unlocked.
